---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { ADSENSE_CLIENT, AMAZON_DISCLOSURE, AMAZON_TAG, BUTTONDOWN_USERNAME, CF_ANALYTICS_TOKEN, CONTACT_EMAIL, OPERATOR_NAME } from '../site/settings.js';

const UPDATED = '21 October 2026';
---

<Base title="Privacy policy" description="What personal data Bradbury Challenge processes and your rights.">
  <article class="prose">
    <h1 class="page-title">Privacy policy</h1>
    <p class="updated">Last updated: {UPDATED}</p>

    <h2>Who is responsible</h2>
    <p>
      Bradbury Challenge (bradburychallenge.org) is an independent project. The controller of the personal data described
      here is {OPERATOR_NAME ?? 'its editor'}, who can be reached at{' '}
      <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>What we do not collect</h2>
    {
      BUTTONDOWN_USERNAME ? (
        <p>
          There are no accounts. The only personal data we ask for is your email address, and only if you choose to
          subscribe to the newsletter (see below). We do not sell or share personal data.
        </p>
      ) : (
        <p>
          There are no accounts, no forms and no newsletter. We do not ask for your name or email address, and we do
          not sell or share personal data.
        </p>
      )
    }

    {
      BUTTONDOWN_USERNAME && (
        <>
          <h2>Newsletter</h2>
          <p>
            If you subscribe to the daily email, your address is stored by Buttondown, the service that sends it, and
            used only to send you the readings. You will be asked to confirm your subscription by email, and every email
            has a link to unsubscribe at once. We process your address because you asked for the newsletter (consent,
            Article 6(1)(a) GDPR), and we keep it until you unsubscribe. Buttondown may record whether emails are opened
            and which links are clicked; see <a href="https://buttondown.com/legal/privacy">Buttondown's privacy policy</a>.
          </p>
        </>
      )
    }

    <h2>Your reading marks</h2>
    <p>
      When you tick a reading as read, the mark is stored in your own browser (local storage). It never leaves your
      device and we cannot see it. Clearing your browser data removes it.
    </p>

    <h2>Hosting</h2>
    <p>
      The site is served by Cloudflare. Like any web server, Cloudflare processes your IP address and basic request
      data to deliver the pages and protect them from abuse. This is necessary to run the site (legitimate interest,
      Article 6(1)(f) GDPR). See <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/">Cloudflare's privacy policy</a>.
    </p>

    {
      CF_ANALYTICS_TOKEN && (
        <>
          <h2>Visitor statistics</h2>
          <p>
            We count visits with Cloudflare Web Analytics, which uses no cookies and does not track you across sites or
            build a profile of you. We only see aggregate figures such as page views and countries.
          </p>
        </>
      )
    }

    <h2>Advertising</h2>
    {
      ADSENSE_CLIENT ? (
        <>
          <p>
            The site is funded by advertising from Google AdSense. Google and its partners may use cookies and similar
            technologies to show ads, measure them and, if you agree, personalise them. Visitors in the European Economic
            Area, the United Kingdom and Switzerland are asked for consent first, through Google's consent management
            platform, which follows the IAB Transparency and Consent Framework. If you refuse, Google may still show
            non-personalised or limited ads, which use cookies only for purposes such as fraud prevention and frequency
            capping, as its policies allow.
          </p>
          <p>
            You can change your choices at any time with the <strong>Privacy settings</strong> link at the bottom of every
            page. See <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites">how Google uses information from sites
            that use its services</a>.
          </p>
        </>
      ) : (
        <p>The site does not show advertising at the moment. If that changes, this policy will be updated first.</p>
      )
    }

    <h2>Affiliate links and contributions</h2>
    <p>
      The Read and Write pages link to Amazon. {AMAZON_TAG ? <>{AMAZON_DISCLOSURE}{' '}</> : ''}If you follow one of those
      links, Amazon may use cookies on its own site to record that the visit came from here; we receive no personal data
      about you, only aggregate figures on purchases. The Buy me a coffee page links to Ko-fi, an external payment service whose
      own privacy policy applies to any contribution you make there.
    </p>

    <h2>Links to other sites</h2>
    <p>
      Every reading opens on the site of its publisher. Those sites have their own privacy policies, which apply once you
      are there.
    </p>

    <h2>Your rights</h2>
    <p>
      Under the GDPR you have the right to access, correct or erase your personal data, to object to or restrict its
      processing, and to withdraw consent at any time. Write to <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>. You
      can also complain to a data protection authority; in Portugal, the Comissão Nacional de Proteção de Dados
      (<a href="https://www.cnpd.pt/">cnpd.pt</a>).
    </p>

    <p>See also the <a href="/cookies/">cookie policy</a>.</p>
  </article>
</Base>
